<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  EPIC-33 — `ring_single`: the Readiness ring. Mirrors iOS's RingSingleWidget, which ships as a
  `.systemSmall` Home Screen widget, so the Android target is the 2x2 cell that is the closest
  equivalent the launcher grid offers.

  See ring_single's <receiver> in AndroidManifest.xml for why these five providers exist now, ahead
  of the Glance dependency, and why swapping the receiver's superclass later leaves this file
  untouched.

  `updatePeriodMillis="0"` disables the platform's own alarm-driven refresh. It is not "never
  update": the floor the platform enforces is 30 minutes regardless of what is asked for, and it
  wakes the app on a schedule BADAN does not control. Widgets are refreshed instead from the same
  places the data actually changes — the ingestion pipeline and the WorkManager sync — which is
  both cheaper and the only way a widget can be correct within seconds of a new reading rather than
  within half an hour of one.

  `widgetCategory` is `home_screen` alone. iOS's Lock Screen / StandBy accessory families have no
  Android counterpart — keyguard widgets left the platform after API 21 — and the honest Android
  surface for the same need is the Wear tile set (see wear_tile_* in strings.xml).
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:resizeMode="none"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_initial_loading"
    android:description="@string/widget_ring_single_description"
    tools:targetApi="31" />
